-- A rule that reads a section binder, passed as a value.
--
-- Discharge gives such a rule an extra input for the binder, which a bare
-- mention of its name cannot carry -- so the reference is eta-expanded into the
-- function the writer meant, `GIVEN _eta0 YIELD bump _eta0 `the rate``. Passing
-- a reader to `map` is ordinary L4 and has to keep working.

IMPORT prelude

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
bump n MEANS n TIMES `the rate`

-- The bare name, passed straight to a higher-order function.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`all bumped` MEANS map bump (LIST 1, 2, 3)

-- The explicit lambda, which meant the same thing before and still does.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`all bumped the long way` MEANS map (GIVEN x YIELD bump x) (LIST 1, 2, 3)

#EVAL `all bumped` WITH `the rate` IS 10
#EVAL `all bumped the long way` WITH `the rate` IS 10

#ASSERT (`all bumped` WITH `the rate` IS 10) EQUALS (LIST 10, 20, 30)
#ASSERT (`all bumped the long way` WITH `the rate` IS 10) EQUALS (LIST 10, 20, 30)
